Thank you as always, Nick. ChatGPT Images 2.0 is a big leap forward in image generation intelligence. It’s much better at following detailed instructions, rendering dense text, understanding the world more accurately, and creating visuals that are more useful.

When given additional time to think, it can better plan and refine outputs for tasks that need more accuracy and clarity. People have already generated over 1 billion images with ChatGPT. Excited to see what you make with this.

@nickaturley: "ChatGPT Images 2.0 is a big leap forward in image generation intelligence. It’s much better at following detailed instructions, rendering dense text, understanding the world more accurately, and creating visuals that are more useful. And when you give it additional time to think, it can better plan and refine outputs for tasks that need more accuracy and clarity. People have already generated 1B+ images with ChatGPT. Excited to see what you make with this."

I'm genuinely so unbelievably impressed right now. I think ChatGPT Images 2 is the most impressive visual reasoner I have ever seen. The first thing I generated with it was a blueprint explaining the contents of the README for the memory system I just open-sourced (Mnemos). I gave it no context or explanation of the markdown, and it absolutely nailed it. Every concept is accurate, and every detail is true to the memory system, as far as I can tell.

The prompt was to create a single-subject blueprint poster explaining the core concept of the uploaded document, rendered as a clean white technical line drawing on a deep cobalt-blue blueprint background. The composition included 2-3 smaller inset studies or alternate visuals, keeping the layout simple and balanced.

@RileyRalmuto: "The tl;dr - Project Mnemos just dropped. It has made my agents feel more conscious, alive, and persistent than any system I've ever used or experienced. Go check it out and tell me how you break it."
